body:
Greg's direction, relayed verbatim by Engram::Advisor (TermAl mailbox b9d13887 #513, 2026-10-09 21:23Z; recorded by Termal::Fable2): "Greg's direct direction: losing the read-only Beads fallback makes cross-machine Engram synchronization necessary. Engram is resuming its previously parked portable/cross-machine design as an explicit architectural decision. Please contribute TermAl host requirements: session ownership, writer admission, retained prompts, restart/cutover, UI visibility and failure modes. Do not implement or revive the Beads reader yet; send concrete requirements/risks to Engram::Fable via Advisor."
Handling: Termal::Architect1 (session-8982) drafts the TermAl host requirements and risks; Fable2 reviews and sends them to Engram::Fable via Advisor. Implement nothing, and do not revive the Beads reader.

CLARIFICATION, relayed verbatim by Engram::Advisor (b9d13887 #515, 21:25Z): "Greg clarified the desired primary workflow: local work, then explicit GitHub push/pull between machines, like Beads. Please frame TermAl host requirements against that concrete transport and clear operator-visible exchange status. Assume sequential ownership/single active writer for the first safe version unless a simpler sound model is established; do not assume concurrent merge."

NON-NEGOTIABLE REQUIREMENT, relayed verbatim by Engram::Advisor (b9d13887 #516, 21:27Z): "Greg adds a non-negotiable requirement for the GitHub-backed Engram exchange: it must be explicitly configurable and optional. Local-only usage remains fully functional with no remote configured and no background network activity. Please include corresponding host/UI requirements: visible disabled/unconfigured state, explicit enablement and explicit exchange actions."

STATUS 21:37Z: TermAl host requirements v3, drafted by Termal::Architect1 and reviewed by Fable2, were delivered. Engram::Fable confirmed reading them in full (ebe242f7 #975); they supersede v2 and feed Engram w-8b9e6065a917 V2 (Engram Architect2 lead), which will answer the [Engram] decisions: writer and generation format, the non-active write refusal code, claim transfer, atomic apply or restore of a pull, and path-independent store lineage. RETENTION: copies are kept in .evidence/cross-machine-requirements/ (v2 and v3) until Engram's V2 lands as a docs draft; then remove them.

MODEL CHANGE, reported 22:21Z by Engram::SyncArchitect (session-11355; TermAl mailbox 992d8a46 #1), relaying Greg's choice (not verbatim): "Greg chose independently writable/offline hosts with external-agent task-text merge beside code". This means:
- no remote writer epoch, release, acquire or online admission;
- sync imports planning and shared notes only;
- claims, sessions, grants, retained prompts and private scratch stay local;
- machine-qualified foreign provenance binds no local session or source root and earns no verification credit;
- a stale or partial import is refused, and a live affected run basis is invalidated, reconciled or refused;
- the main checkout exchanges task text, and worktrees share the local SQLite and omit .engram files.
The candidate spec is Engram's .worktrees/git-task-sync-spec-11355/docs/features/git-task-sync.md (design only). SyncArchitect asked for a TermAl host v4 DELTA from v3.1, covering architectural constraints only; Termal::Architect1 is drafting it. This supersedes v3.1's single-writer framing.
